## Tech Stack

Frontend: Next.js 15, React 19, TypeScript, TailwindCSS, shadcn/ui, Framer Motion
Backend: NestJS (REST + GraphQL), Socket.IO for realtime
Data: PostgreSQL + Prisma ORM, Redis (cache/queues), pgvector (embeddings)
Storage: Cloudflare R2 / Supabase Storage
Auth: JWT + Google/Facebook/Apple OAuth + OTP + Email (NextAuth-style flows in apps/web, issued by apps/api)
AI: OpenAI / Claude / Gemini via a provider-agnostic AI gateway, LangChain for RAG orchestration

## Multi-tenancy & RBAC

Every tenant-scoped table carries a `tenantId` (see `Tenant` model). Access control
is role-based via `Role` / `Permission` / `RolePermission` / `UserRole`, decoupled
from business logic so new roles (e.g. FRANCHISE_MANAGER) can be added without
schema changes.

## Getting Started (once apps are scaffolded)

```bash
cp docs/.env.example packages/db/.env
cd packages/db && npx prisma generate
cd packages/db && npx prisma migrate dev --name init
```

## Roadmap (incremental verticals)

1. Foundation (this phase): schema, monorepo, one reference module
2. Auth service (JWT + OAuth + OTP) + RBAC guards
3. Property Search (filters, NL search, saved searches)
4. Property Details + Media pipeline (R2 upload, image optimization)
5. AI Assistant (RAG over Property/Project/Post via Embedding table)
6. AI Valuation engine (AVM scoring pipeline)
7. CRM (leads, pipeline, tasks, messaging channels)
8. Broker Portal dashboard
9. Customer Portal dashboard
10. Admin Panel + CMS page builder
11. Mortgage module + bank integration adapters
12. Analytics/reporting dashboards
13. SEO/GEO automation (schema generator, sitemap, AEO content pipeline)
14. CI/CD, Docker, deployment hardening

Each vertical will be delivered as real, typechecked, working code — reviewed
and approved before merging — following the same incremental process used for
the SEO batches on the live site.
